Cell["\<\
1. Open this .nb notebook in Mathematica and evaluate this input
   cell (Shift+Enter).
2. Alternatively, evaluate it from another notebook:

   NotebookEvaluate[\"/path/to/PlotOptions.nb\"];

   If both notebooks are in the same directory:

   NotebookEvaluate[FileNameJoin[{NotebookDirectory[], \"PlotOptions.nb\"}]];

The settings apply to the current Mathematica kernel session.
The notebook sets frame, axes, grid-line, and label styles for
common 2D plots, and defines palettes such as RGBString and
RGBStringAlternative115. It also configures MaTeX for LaTeX labels.\
\>", "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{4.0036516302251225`*^9, 4.0036516312254105`*^9}, {
  4.003651687177412*^9, 4.0036517000526905`*^9}, {4.0036517360986023`*^9, 
